  "// Note6": "Every page the site publishes is listed below (one URL per route, 15 Nov 2026), so a new violation on any page fails CI. Pages from public/ that are plain HTML (_designs, wireframes, offline.html) have no footer, so they skip the footer wait. Auth-gated pages redirect to the sign-in screen and are audited as that screen. The /404 and unknown-route pages are left out.",
  "// Note7": "/blog/tags/next.js is left out because the static file server in CI reads the .js ending as a script file; the live-site axe pass covers it. /wireframes and /_designs are galleries of iframes, so axe's frame-tested check is ignored there; each framed page is listed on its own.",
  "// Note8": "/conversations is left out because it only redirects to /messages?tab=chats; in the static export its first HTML is Next's redirect shell, which has no lang attribute until the browser follows the redirect. /messages is listed on its own."
